Every command has a "signature", which is a list of tagged elements.
Attempting to use the empty string as a signature is an error.  (The
correct signature to indicate "no parameters" is ":void".)  Every
element must be tagged with a `:' tag; any NAME prefix is optional.


Tags:

:filename       Like :rest, I guess.  Path is stripped of "quotes" and <brackets>
:int            Integer
:optional       Item may or may not appear
:repeat         Last element (not :rest) can be repeated an aribitrary # of additional times
:rest           Arbitrary text, consumes rest of command line
:string         Any series of non-whitespace chars, a single value
:symbol         String of letters/numbers which should be a Symbol name with optional Key
:void           Command takes no parameters; only valid singly


These are immediate:

@array          ARR:symbol
@break          :void
@case           NAME:symbol
@continue       :void
@define         NAME:symbol :optional TEXT:rest
@else           :void
@endcase        :void
@endcmd         :void
@endif          :void
@endlong        :void
@endlongdef     :void
@endwhile       :void
@esac           :void
@fi             :void
@for            VAR:symbol START:int END:int :optional INCR:int
@foreach        VAR:symbol NAME:symbol
@if             EXPR:rest
@list           LIS:symbol
@local          NAME:symbol
@longdef        NAME:symbol
@newcmd         NAME:symbol :optional SPEC:rest
@next           VAR:symbol
@of             TEXT:rest
@otherwise      :void
@return         :optional VALUE:rest
@set            NAME:symbol :optional TEXT:rest
@sm2ctl         TEXT:rest
@unless         EXPR:rest
@until          EXPR:rest
@wend           :void
@while          EXPR:rest


These are not:

@append         NAME:symbol TEXT:rest
@cleardivert    :optional :repeat N:int
# @comment        ?? :optional TEXT:rest         Removed from input stream by the parser, but perhaps it shouldn't be
@data           LIS:symbol
@debug          :optional TEXT:rest
@decr           NAME:symbol :optional N:int
@default        NAME:symbol VAL:rest
@divert         :optional N:int
@divpop         :void
@divpush        N:int
@dump           :optional WHAT:string :optional FILE:filename
@dumpall        :optional WHAT:string :optional FILE:filename
@dumpdef        :optional :repeat SYM:symbol
@echo           :optional TEXT:rest
@enddata        :void
@error          :optional TEXT:rest
@eod            :void
@error          :optional TEXT:rest
@errprint       :optional TEXT:rest
@esyscmd        CMDLINE:rest
@eval           TEXT:rest
@exit           :optional N:int
@filedata       LIS:symbol FILE:filename
@filedef        NAME:symbol FILE:filename
@filedefine     NAME:symbol FILE:filename
@ignore         PATTERN:rest
@import         LIB:symbol FILE:filename
@include        FILE:filename
@incr           NAME:symbol :optional N:int
@initialize     NAME:symbol VAL:rest
@input          :optional NAME:symbol
@m2ctl          TEXT:rest
@literal        PATTERN:rest
@namespace      NAMESPACE:symbol
@nextfile       :void
@nsinclude      FILE:filename
@paste          FILE:filename
@readonly       NAME:symbol
@secho          :optional TEXT:rest
@sequence       ID:symbol ACTION:string :optional ARG:rest
@serror         :optional TEXT:rest
@sexit          :optional N:int
@sfiledata
@sfiledef
@sfiledefine
@shell          PATTERN:string :optional PROG:rest
@simport
@sinclude
@snsinclude
@spaste
@split          NAME:symbol LIS:symbol :optional FS:string
@syscmd         CMDLINE:rest
@tracemode      :optional FLAG:string
@traceoff       :optional :repeat SYM:symbol
@traceon        :optional :repeat SYM:symbol
@typeout        :void
@undef
@undefine       NAME:symbol
# @undivert       :optional :repeat N:int
#  -or-
# @undivert       N:int FILE:filename
@undivert       :optional N:int :optional N__FILE:rest
@warn
@wrap           TEXT:rest
